= Reference — Simple =

'''Reference''' is how a word, name, sign, or act of communication points to or talks about something.

The name “Mars” can refer to the planet Mars. The word “I” refers to different people depending on who says it.

Reference is not the same thing as meaning. Two names can refer to the same thing while giving a listener different information.

Reference is also different from [[Identity/Simple|identity]]. Identity is about whether two things are actually the same thing. Reference is about how an expression is connected to what it talks about.

[[Context (linguistics)/Simple|Context]] often helps determine reference, especially for words such as “I”, “here”, “now”, “this”, and “that”.

